WEBVTT

00:06.710 --> 00:08.360
A long, long time ago...

00:08.360 --> 00:11.280
The Gods of the skies, known as the Heavenly People,

00:11.970 --> 00:16.500
fought a huge war against the humans of the Lower World.

00:19.700 --> 00:24.040
It was a battle fought over the almighty power that can create anything-

00:25.200 --> 00:27.590
the Akuto.

02:46.120 --> 02:48.410
Tanaka-sensei, over there!

02:48.410 --> 02:50.950
What are they doing?

03:03.430 --> 03:04.300
Suzume!

03:08.230 --> 03:09.550
Suzuki-sensei...

03:10.230 --> 03:12.050
Hurry up and call the fire department!

03:12.050 --> 03:12.930
Okay!

03:13.650 --> 03:15.720
Imamura! Takamori!

03:15.720 --> 03:17.950
Dying won't solve anything, so come back!

03:25.530 --> 03:26.400
No way!

03:26.400 --> 03:27.990
Yumemi, over there!

03:27.990 --> 03:28.990
Suzume?

03:33.420 --> 03:35.510
What are you doing, Suzume?

03:37.050 --> 03:41.250
Kazuya-kun said their future would begin there.

03:41.250 --> 03:43.880
So they're trying to overcome something together.

03:46.680 --> 03:48.510
Suzume!

03:47.060 --> 03:50.570
Kazuya-kun! Suzume! Good luck!

04:03.820 --> 04:05.580
Lady Ryuely, what is that thing?

04:07.330 --> 04:12.700
It is an irrevocable mistake that the
Heavenly beings made a long time ago.

04:13.420 --> 04:16.110
We tried to look for more Akuto because we used our own up.

04:16.110 --> 04:20.410
So we crossed the space-time continuum into countless different planets.

04:20.410 --> 04:24.460
We took the futures of those creatures away without mercy.

04:25.090 --> 04:28.190
Sometimes, we even had to use that thing.

04:29.510 --> 04:32.070
But why is it attacking Lord Munto?

04:32.750 --> 04:37.240
Munto is now facing a past that the
Heavenly people should've made up for.

04:39.150 --> 04:41.840
He is shouldering all our sins...

04:41.840 --> 04:43.410
...by himself.

04:50.910 --> 04:52.770
Are you all right, Suzume?

04:52.770 --> 04:54.070
Yeah, I'm fine!

04:54.070 --> 04:55.360
Just a little bit more.

04:55.360 --> 04:56.570
Don't let go of my hand.

04:56.570 --> 04:57.260
Okay.

04:59.290 --> 05:01.620
Suzume looks really happy.

05:02.260 --> 05:04.610
Yeah, it's strange.

05:04.610 --> 05:06.420
Even though she always seems so unreliable...

05:07.340 --> 05:10.940
Even though we always think that she needs our protection...

05:11.240 --> 05:17.600
Now that I think about it, Suzume might actually be the one supporting <i>me</i>.

05:18.190 --> 05:21.350
She never fails to keep us on the edge of our seats, though.

05:22.190 --> 05:26.960
When Suzume is here, I feel calm and relaxed.

05:34.200 --> 05:39.340
When I was a second grader in elementary school, I was in the same class as Suzume.

05:40.590 --> 05:47.250
During that summer, our class was going on a field trip to a hillside park in a neighboring town.

05:48.300 --> 05:51.610
But on that morning, I couldn't go because I suddenly came down with a fever.

05:52.160 --> 05:56.150
My mom had something to do
outside, so I was home by myself.

05:56.600 --> 06:00.220
The house was <i>really empty...</i>

06:00.900 --> 06:04.850
It felt as if everyone had abandoned me and gone off to a faraway place...

06:06.040 --> 06:09.650
I thought to myself, "What will happen if I'm alone forever?"

06:10.460 --> 06:13.530
Then I felt really sad and I was about to burst into tears.

06:14.450 --> 06:15.570
Then...

06:26.510 --> 06:28.880
Although I didn't notice back then...

06:29.350 --> 06:32.360
Suzume heard about me from the teacher...

06:32.960 --> 06:37.320
...and she walked back from the neighboring town by herself.

06:39.230 --> 06:41.950
Even though Suzume didn't say anything about it,

06:41.950 --> 06:50.100
I knew she had to have walked kilometers back
from that faraway park by herself, just for my sake.

06:51.740 --> 06:55.940
She must have gotten lost along the way...

06:57.540 --> 06:58.780
Moved back...

06:59.830 --> 07:01.030
Headed forward...

07:02.750 --> 07:04.740
Then went around in circles...

07:05.380 --> 07:09.830
Despite that, she didn't give up, but continued to search...

07:09.830 --> 07:11.460
...until she found me.

07:13.390 --> 07:18.690
The day before, I had promised
Suzume that I'd eat lunch with her.

07:19.270 --> 07:23.200
She said, "Let's eat together! I'm looking forward to it!"

07:25.520 --> 07:32.210
We need to believe in her because she has never doubted us.

07:33.240 --> 07:36.750
She knows things that are important to us...

07:38.510 --> 07:40.470
...and she's trying to protect them.

07:41.710 --> 07:42.740
Suzume...

07:44.830 --> 07:45.620
But...

07:46.710 --> 07:50.080
Even if that's the case, she should've thought it over more carefully!

07:50.080 --> 07:51.960
She's being too reckless!

07:51.960 --> 07:53.560
Suzume!

08:10.320 --> 08:11.390
Run!

08:17.950 --> 08:19.050
Suzume!

08:34.840 --> 08:35.900
Yes!

08:36.280 --> 08:37.400
Are you okay?

08:38.180 --> 08:38.920
Yeah.

08:47.610 --> 08:50.470
There's only one pillar left...

08:51.360 --> 08:52.250
Munto...

09:04.750 --> 09:07.780
It doesn't seem like they're trying to commit suicide.

09:07.780 --> 09:09.030
Yeah...

09:09.030 --> 09:13.180
But where are they planning to go?

09:13.180 --> 09:16.000
I believe it's the shore on the other-

09:20.220 --> 09:21.260
Over there!

09:21.260 --> 09:22.550
It's Suzume!

09:22.550 --> 09:23.800
Isn't that Kazuya?

09:23.800 --> 09:25.430
What are they doing?

09:25.430 --> 09:27.300
Kazuya is trying to start something!

09:27.300 --> 09:29.380
Good luck, Suzume!

09:29.380 --> 09:30.200
Don't drown!

09:30.930 --> 09:32.270
Go!

09:32.270 --> 09:33.800
Kazuya-kun!

09:33.800 --> 09:36.290
Hey, you guys! Go back to school!

09:45.250 --> 09:48.230
Suzume, hold on!

09:48.230 --> 09:50.890
You can do it, Suzume!

09:51.190 --> 09:52.240
Yumemi.

09:51.590 --> 09:53.890
Just a little bit more, Kazuya, Suzume!

09:52.880 --> 09:53.890
Mom...

09:54.800 --> 09:56.890
Is that Suzume-chan?

10:24.540 --> 10:26.280
It's useless, Gass.

10:27.000 --> 10:31.430
A lone pillar isn't enough to hold up the entire Magical Kingdom.

10:33.590 --> 10:34.660
I know.

10:35.170 --> 10:38.170
This country was destined to fall.

10:38.840 --> 10:42.330
However, this is not limited to the Magical Kingdom.

10:42.330 --> 10:45.550
The Heavens will also sink into darkness.

10:46.100 --> 10:50.250
We cannot change that fate.

10:50.250 --> 10:54.140
Guardian of Space and Time, Outsider Gass.

10:54.140 --> 10:56.950
Are you planning to abandon the Heavens, too?

11:00.910 --> 11:03.710
Have you ever had a dream?

11:03.710 --> 11:04.730
Dream?

11:10.580 --> 11:12.870
The attacks on all pillars are complete!

11:13.600 --> 11:15.910
The Magical Kingdom is beginning to fall.

11:16.350 --> 11:18.180
Gass, run!

11:49.880 --> 11:52.200
Yay!

11:53.890 --> 11:55.030
She did it!

11:55.030 --> 11:56.200
Suzume!

11:57.920 --> 11:59.200
Thank goodness!

12:31.870 --> 12:33.200
Munto.

12:34.330 --> 12:37.910
You and your country shall disappear.

12:48.690 --> 12:52.300
I know you guys wanted to try something extraordinary,

12:52.300 --> 12:54.240
and we had no intentions of stopping you.

12:54.240 --> 12:59.360
But you're students, so you should have done something more appropriate for students!

12:59.360 --> 13:01.490
For example... Study or join a club...

13:01.490 --> 13:03.660
You made a lot of people worry...

13:05.920 --> 13:09.500
Their future has just begun.

13:31.860 --> 13:33.600
Yumemi, what's wrong?

13:36.410 --> 13:38.060
Ichiko, am I...

13:38.910 --> 13:41.240
...able to protect everyone's future?

13:41.560 --> 13:42.440
Huh?

13:42.440 --> 13:45.780
Even though I didn't understand anything he said...

13:45.780 --> 13:49.770
If what I see is truly our future...

13:49.770 --> 13:52.410
I can't allow it to happen!

13:53.170 --> 13:53.990
Yumemi?

13:53.990 --> 13:55.550
Ichiko! Mom!

13:56.000 --> 13:58.890
I have to protect everyone's future!

14:00.140 --> 14:02.180
Yumemi, where are you going?!

14:07.770 --> 14:09.390
Hey, look at that!

14:09.390 --> 14:10.790
What is it?

14:10.790 --> 14:12.140
You've got to be kidding!

14:12.140 --> 14:13.150
A UFO?

14:14.070 --> 14:14.890
Seriously?

14:14.890 --> 14:16.010
It's huge...

14:16.010 --> 14:17.230
Is it real?

14:17.230 --> 14:18.220
No way...

14:18.220 --> 14:19.160
It has to be a cloud!

14:20.010 --> 14:21.160
That is...

14:22.160 --> 14:23.990
What's happening to the sky?

14:23.990 --> 14:25.660
Is it a plane?

14:26.070 --> 14:29.020
No, it's too big...

14:29.020 --> 14:31.170
Should we ask the weather department?

14:32.460 --> 14:36.670
Kazuya, this is the sky that Yumemi sees.

14:38.300 --> 14:40.180
This is Yumemi's sky.

14:41.220 --> 14:46.130
Oba-san, Yumemi had always seen floating islands like this in the sky.

14:46.810 --> 14:49.300
She's seen them ever since she was young!

14:49.940 --> 14:50.600
I...

14:50.970 --> 14:52.130
Ichiko-chan...

14:52.130 --> 14:56.690
I believed her, but I couldn't see any of them until now.

14:56.880 --> 14:58.100
It was really frustrating...

14:59.950 --> 15:02.650
But now I can finally see them!

15:03.160 --> 15:04.700
I'm really happy!

15:06.160 --> 15:06.950
Ichiko-chan...

15:07.360 --> 15:10.820
I'll bring Yumemi back, so don't worry.

15:18.340 --> 15:22.000
I first saw them when I was about five.

15:22.970 --> 15:29.470
I just took it for granted that numerous islands were floating beyond the clouds,

15:30.520 --> 15:35.310
just like the natural existence of the sky and the clouds themselves.

15:35.940 --> 15:39.690
Being so young, I thought the islands were a natural thing, too.

15:42.950 --> 15:47.490
After a few years passed, I realized that no one else was able to see them.

15:48.830 --> 15:50.610
Where are they?

15:50.610 --> 15:52.290
What is she talking about?

15:52.290 --> 15:53.190
They're really there.

15:53.190 --> 15:53.880
I'm not lying.

15:54.370 --> 15:55.860
What nonsense!

15:55.860 --> 15:58.700
Yumemi is an idiot who dreams even when she's awake!

15:58.700 --> 16:01.080
Yumemi is a liar!

16:01.080 --> 16:02.960
Hey, tell me about it!

16:03.760 --> 16:05.600
Do they really exist?

16:06.030 --> 16:07.550
Where are they?

16:07.550 --> 16:09.350
I want to see them too!

16:12.560 --> 16:13.460
Over there...

16:13.460 --> 16:15.650
Oh, there are a lot of clouds today!

16:18.270 --> 16:22.940
Ever since then, I tried not to think too much about the sky.

16:25.740 --> 16:27.950
I'm different from everyone else.

16:29.120 --> 16:30.990
I was afraid of that.

16:32.000 --> 16:34.240
I wish I had never known about them.

16:34.960 --> 16:37.960
I was afraid of myself because I was different.

16:38.460 --> 16:40.540
I tried to think of it as a dream.

16:41.720 --> 16:43.700
I tried to forget about it.

16:43.700 --> 16:47.740
Even now, I still want to run away from it.

16:47.740 --> 16:50.090
But... but...

16:51.770 --> 16:53.300
...this isn't a dream!

16:54.060 --> 16:55.680
I can't go on like this!

16:58.690 --> 17:02.490
I have to protect everyone's future!

17:12.160 --> 17:12.700
Munto!

17:15.580 --> 17:17.920
So you came, Yumemi...

17:23.010 --> 17:25.090
Hold on! Don't disappear!

17:25.570 --> 17:26.910
Hurry!

17:26.910 --> 17:32.200
Your voice made it past the space-time continuum to me.

17:32.200 --> 17:35.520
It is proof that you hold the power to open up the future...

17:35.840 --> 17:38.600
...and that you are the Girl of Destiny!

17:39.140 --> 17:45.610
We both share the same fate and we both have the power to regenerate the cycle of Akuto.

17:46.400 --> 17:48.640
I believe you, Munto.

17:48.640 --> 17:51.940
I believe in you and in my own power!

18:12.640 --> 18:14.060
Lady Ryuely, look!

18:14.340 --> 18:17.440
Who is that person?!

18:17.760 --> 18:19.940
This is...

18:22.900 --> 18:23.400
Yumemi!

18:36.450 --> 18:37.620
Munto...

18:39.420 --> 18:42.910
There is a huge space-time distortion in the Lower World!

18:43.280 --> 18:45.050
This is unbelievable!

18:45.050 --> 18:46.880
This is coming from a source outside the space-time continuum!

18:48.090 --> 18:53.880
This is done by someone who's <i>not a Heavenly Being!</i>

18:55.720 --> 19:01.980
She's getting nearer and nearer even though the repellent force is as great as a planet's!

19:02.470 --> 19:05.670
Look! She doesn't have any equipment on her!

19:05.670 --> 19:08.570
She's crossing through time by herself...

19:09.050 --> 19:12.440
So this is Munto's goal?!

19:13.370 --> 19:16.410
She is the Girl of...

19:22.460 --> 19:23.530
Munto!

19:39.980 --> 19:41.140
Munto, give me your hand!

19:42.190 --> 19:43.550
You can't disappear!

19:43.550 --> 19:44.110
Munto!

19:44.640 --> 19:49.110
How many times do I have to tell you that it's "Lord Munto"?!

19:51.400 --> 19:52.740
Munto...

20:14.050 --> 20:17.580
For a moment, the two worlds connected...

20:17.580 --> 20:20.720
...and the enormous power that was trapped in both sides...

20:20.720 --> 20:25.350
...was released from our hands and spilled into both worlds.

20:26.400 --> 20:29.230
I wonder what happened after that?

20:30.150 --> 20:35.360
When I woke up, I only saw Ichiko trying to wake me up.

20:36.620 --> 20:40.580
I finally saw the floating islands you always talked about.

20:48.210 --> 20:52.960
At that moment, the whole world was able to see the floating islands.

20:53.630 --> 20:57.670
Everyone saw the same sky that I see.

20:58.850 --> 21:01.090
But it was over quickly.

21:01.090 --> 21:07.680
Now, a lot of scientists are researching
and hypothesizing about what occurred.

21:08.860 --> 21:11.130
I wonder if Munto is okay...

21:11.130 --> 21:14.200
Did the cycle of Akuto recover?

21:14.650 --> 21:19.150
Unfortunately, I don't think the world returned to its original state.

21:20.660 --> 21:25.360
But I believe that, even if it was for just a moment,

21:25.360 --> 21:28.710
everyone in the world saw the same sky that I see.

21:29.540 --> 21:33.790
That's why, one day, I believe we'll definitely meet again...

24:32.230 --> 24:33.670
It's finally my turn.

24:33.670 --> 24:35.230
Twenty second previews go by really fast.

24:35.680 --> 24:37.920
The Heavens are in chaos,

24:37.920 --> 24:42.140
but I will head to the Lower World and make sure the Akuto source is safe.

24:42.140 --> 24:45.640
Next episode of The World Reflected in the Eyes of a Girl who Looks Up at the Sky:

24:45.640 --> 24:46.980
Yearning.

24:46.980 --> 24:48.620
How was it? Did it go in?
